   "duty": "ED26-P15-CH-measure-extension-C008 (partial): The 'construction or argument' and the 'full treatment promised by its declared status' (proved=annex:p15.stieltjes-construction) are not fully supplied. In handbook/annex/p15/measure-extension.tex, the endpoint-limit step (lines 288-296) writes only the lower end (inf F is the limit at minus infinity). It disposes of the upper end with 'The upper-end proof is the reversed argument' (line 296), which is a 'similarly'-type elision. The unwritten upper-end fact is that F(n) increases to F(inf)=sup F, including when sup F is infinite. The proof uses it at lines 383-385 and 387-391 to truncate targets with b = infinity. So the following all depend on a step that is not written: the countable covering bound for unbounded targets (395-399), the second partition condition, the premeasure, existence of mu_F with mu_F(I(a,inf))=F(inf)-F(a), and mu_F(R)=F(inf)-F(-inf) (401-407). C008 becomes covered once the upper-end case is written out.",
